  "id": "DrugBank_DB00620 - MONDO_grouped_6545_44719",
  "verbalization": "Tiamcinolone, a corticosteroid, is associated with Erythema Multiforme through a chain of indications involving Hydrocortisone Acetate. The evidence suggests that Triamcinolone may be used in conditions that are linked to Hydrocortisone Acetate, which in turn is linked to Erythema Multiforme. This pathway implies a potential mechanism where corticosteroids, such as Hydrocortisone Acetate, are used in the treatment of inflammatory or autoimmune conditions, and their use may contribute to the development of Erythema Multiforme. The recurring involvement of Hydrocortisone Acetate in multiple pathways highlights its role as a mediator in the relationship between Triamcinolone and Erythema Multiforme. The evidence suggests a possible dependency on corticosteroids in the pathogenesis of Erythema Multiforme, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
